{
  "id": "ep018",
  "duration": 54.532,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.6,
      "text": "A single orbital collision could trap humanity on Earth for centuries.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Debris-LEO1280.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA employee",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debris-LEO1280.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.6,
      "end": 10.72,
      "text": "Many believe that space is so vast that satellite accidents are minor, isolated events.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ISS055-E-102134 - View of Earth.jpg",
        "credit": "Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, NASA Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISS055-E-102134_-_View_of_Earth.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.6,
          "end": 7.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 7.667,
          "end": 10.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.72,
      "end": 18.24,
      "text": "But in 1978, NASA scientists Donald Kessler and Burton Cour-Palais revealed a terrifying reality.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.733,
          "end": 18.233,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.24,
      "end": 25.66,
      "text": "At orbit speeds over 17,000 miles per hour, even tiny paint flecks destroy entire spacecraft.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS070-309-029 - STS-070 - Documentation of debris impact damage to flight deck window - DPLA - 2399d521269f3c60723dee49fd204681.jpg",
        "credit": "National Aeronautics and Space Administration. Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center. 2/17/1973",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS070-309-029_-_STS-070_-_Documentation_of_debris_impact_damage_to_flight_deck_window_-_DPLA_-_2399d521269f3c60723dee49fd204681.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.233,
          "end": 20.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.933,
          "end": 25.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.66,
      "end": 31.83,
      "text": "If we cross a critical density of satellites, one crash triggers an autonomous chain reaction.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Gabbard diagram.png",
        "credit": "NASA Orbital Debris Program Office",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gabbard_diagram.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.667,
          "end": 31.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.83,
      "end": 38.33,
      "text": "This cascading debris storm will continue growing even if we completely stop launching rockets.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Growth of space debris.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Growth_of_space_debris.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.833,
          "end": 38.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 38.33,
      "end": 47.05,
      "text": "In 2009, a defunct Russian satellite slammed into an active US satellite, creating thousands of supersonic fragments.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Iridium Satellite.jpg",
        "credit": "Cliff",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iridium_Satellite.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 38.333,
          "end": 47.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 47.05,
      "end": 54.182,
      "text": "This real-world crash proved how easily a single orbital collision could trap humanity on Earth for centuries.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Debris-LEO1280.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA employee",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Debris-LEO1280.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 47.067,
          "end": 54.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
